430
00:37:25.641 --> 00:37:29.881
of progress and innovation that exist alongside injustice and moral

431
00:37:29.881 --> 00:37:34.833
failure. Preserving this building allows us to confront that complexity

432
00:37:34.833 --> 00:37:39.148
head on. It challenges us to engage with the full

433
00:37:39.148 --> 00:37:41.508
scope of our past, not just the parts that are

434
00:37:41.508 --> 00:37:45.534
comfortable. In doing so, we gain a deeper, more honest

435
00:37:45.534 --> 00:37:48.854
understanding of how our community has evolved, how decisions made

436
00:37:48.854 --> 00:37:52.334
generations ago continue to shape our values, built environment and

437
00:37:52.334 --> 00:37:57.198
collective identity. This is the true purpose of heritage conservation,

438
00:37:57.198 --> 00:38:00.238
to preserve the stories that help us grow, reflect, and

439
00:38:00.238 --> 00:38:04.206
strive for a better future. This building tells the story

440
00:38:04.206 --> 00:38:06.566
of far more than one man. It is a living

441
00:38:06.566 --> 00:38:09.326
archive of the many hands, lives and histories that have

442
