00:38:18.858 --> 00:38:21.538
whose names may be lost to history, whose work still

445
00:38:21.538 --> 00:38:25.090
stands as a testament to their artistry. It speaks to

446
00:38:25.090 --> 00:38:28.090
the foundry workers who endured the intense heat and danger

447
00:38:28.090 --> 00:38:31.690
of industrial production forging tools and machinery that would shape

448
00:38:31.690 --> 00:38:36.052
the agricultural landscape of Wellington County. It speaks to the

449
00:38:36.052 --> 00:38:39.652
tools that were cast here. Plows that till the soil,

